  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1233 PM MDT Sun Aug 30 2026\n\nA few isolated showers and storms lingered in the Eastern Highlands \nduring the first half of the day as the cold front made its way \nthrough Eastern Idaho, but the rest of the afternoon and evening is \nexpected to be drier and mild. This afternoon will be the coolest of \nthe next few with highs today in the low to mid 70s across most of \nthe area. Drier air behind the cold front today in combination with \nthe breezy conditions will make for some near-critical to critical \nfire weather conditions for a few hours this afternoon out across \nparts of the eastern Magic Valley and Arco desert area. It's breezy \nacross all of the eastern Magic Valley and Snake River Plain today \nwith gusts of 25 to 35 mph. Sustained winds have been elevated \ntoday, reaching Lake Wind Advisory criteria at times throughout the \nmorning, but are expected to diminish a bit this afternoon. Tonight \nwill be the chilliest night we've had in a while, dropping into the \n30s and 40s.\n\nWe warm up a bit more on Monday and Tuesday with highs ranging from \nmid 70s to mid 80s for many. Monday will be mostly dry, but a weak \nshortwave trough passing through late Monday into Tuesday will bring \nanother small chance for a few isolated showers and storms. While \nthis works through, a deep upper level will be working its way down \nto West Coast. This seems most likely to bring some precipitation \nchances to the Central Mountains on Wednesday, but as it stalls out \nwe could stay drier for the second half of the week. It will help \nkeep our temperatures from warming too quickly, at least, as a cold \nfront passing through will drop highs a few degrees back into the \nmid and upper 70s on Wednesday and Thursday before returning the low \n80s on Friday and Saturday. Look for wind gusts to increase with the \ncold frontal passage on Wednesday, reaching the 25-35 mph range for \nmany. Winds stay breezy each afternoon in the second half of the \nweek, but not quite as breezy as Wednesday.",
